#define R(p,a,r)mix(a*dot(p,a),p,cos(r))+sin(r)*cross(p,a)
#define H(h)cos((h)*6.3+vec3(0,23,21))*.5+.5

// https://iquilezles.org/articles/distfunctions2d
float sdHexagon(vec2 p, float r)
{
    const vec3 k = vec3(-0.866025404,0.5,0.577350269);
    p = abs(p);
    p -= 2.0*min(dot(k.xy,p),0.0)*k.xy;
    p -= vec2(clamp(p.x, -k.z*r, k.z*r), r);
    return length(p)*sign(p.y);
}

float noise_2d(vec2 st)
{
    vec2 i = floor(st);
    vec2 f = fract(st);

    //taking random value from points on a init rect
    float a = rand(i + vec2(0.0, 0.0));
    float b = rand(i + vec2(1.0, 0.0));
    float c = rand(i + vec2(0.0, 1.0));
    float d = rand(i + vec2(1.0, 1.0));

    //Hermite curve interpolation instead of smoothstep because i am a cool kid :)
    vec2 u = f * f * (3.0 - 2.0 * f);
    // u = smoothstep(0.0, 1.0, f);

    return mix(a, b, u.x) + (c - a) * u.y * (1.0 - u.x) + (d - b) * u.x * u.y;
}

#define OCTAVES 8
//Fractal Brownian Motion
float fbm(vec2 st)
{
    float value = 0.0;
    float A = 0.5;

    for (int i = 0; i < OCTAVES; i++)
    {
        value += A * noise_2d(st);
        st *= 1.7;
        A *= 0.55;
    }
    return value;
}
// Constants
#define cell_size 150.0
#define distortion_speed 10.0

// Returns random value in [0, 1) for a given vector
float rand2(vec2 v) {
  return fract(sin(dot(v,vec2(12.98,78.23))) * 21370.2137);
}
// Returns random vector with values in [0, 1) for a given vector
vec2 rand_vec(vec2 v) {
    return vec2(
        fract(sin(dot(v,vec2(12.98,78.23))) * 21370.2137),
        fract(sin(dot(v,vec2(12.98,78.23))) * 21690.4200)
    );
}

// Returns the center of the cell given by x and y
vec2 point_position(float x, float y, float size) {
    vec2 offset_base = rand_vec(vec2(x + 0.5, y + 0.5)) * size * 0.6;
    float freq_mod = rand(vec2(x, y)) + 0.5;
    vec2 offset = offset_base * vec2(
        sin(iTime * distortion_speed * freq_mod / 8.420),
        cos(iTime * distortion_speed * freq_mod / 11.690)
    );
    return vec2((x + 0.5) * size, (y + 0.5) * size) + offset;
}

// Returns a value in [0, 1) representing a cell noise value 
// for a given pixel coord and cell size
float cell_noise(vec2 pixel_coord, float size) {
    float xi = floor(pixel_coord.x / size);
    float yi = floor(pixel_coord.y / size);
    vec2 point_pos = point_position(xi, yi, size);
    float min_distance = size * 2.0;
    for(int i = -1; i < 2; i++) {
        for(int j = -1; j < 2; j++) {
            vec2 point_pos = point_position(xi + float(i), yi + float(j), size);
            min_distance = min(min_distance, distance(pixel_coord, point_pos));
        }
    }
    return smoothstep(0.4, 1.2, min_distance / size);

}

float pattern(vec2 p)
{
    vec2 q = vec2(fbm(p + vec2(0.0, 0.0)), fbm(p + vec2(4.54, 8.3)));
    return fbm(p + q * 5.0);
}

